Design of RiskMeter struct:

```rust
/// The prediction-meter state: how much accumulation has happened toward the
/// dream's ≥5 matched-pair milestone. Computed by counting the two JSONL
/// ledgers. `pairs` uses the same definition as the accuracy report's
/// `lift_events_used` — validation events carrying all three lift fields
/// (predicted_count, total_scored, scored_broke) — so the meter and the
/// `/risk accuracy` "Pairs: N/5" line never disagree.
pub(crate) struct RiskMeter {
    pub(crate) snapshots: usize,
    pub(crate) validations: usize,
    pub(crate) pairs: usize,
    pub(crate) last_snapshot_day: Option<u64>,
    pub(crate) target_pairs: usize,
}
```

Compute function (pure, testable):

```rust
pub(crate) const TARGET_PAIRS: usize = 5;
pub(crate) const RISK_METER_PATH: &str = ".arc/risk_meter.json";

fn is_lift_event(e: &ValidationEvent) -> bool {
    e.predicted_count.is_some() && e.total_scored.is_some() && e.scored_broke.is_some()
}

pub(crate) fn compute_risk_meter(snapshot_content: &str, validation_content: &str) -> RiskMeter {
    let snapshots = parse_all_snapshots(snapshot_content);
    let events = parse_validation_events(validation_content);
    let pairs = events.iter().filter(|e| is_lift_event(e)).count();
